WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:06.060
In every single one of us there is a void
that can never be filled.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:11.620
A part of us that yearns for a complete and
definitive understanding of the life that

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.429
engulfs us.

00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:16.400
An omniscient end point in the pursuit of
knowledge.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.400
At any moment, a new scientific discovery
or technological advancement could occur and

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.400
cause our current conception of reality to
crumble.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.400
And after that, it will just as likely happen
again and again into eternity.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.400
Every answer comes with a new question.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.400
Every step forward illuminates more of a trail
with no destination in sight.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.400
We posses a level of intelligence that seemingly
never meets the needs of the reality that

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.160
precedes it.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.250
We are conscious enough to perceive the world
and add two and twos together.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:33.899
We are conscious enough to ask questions based
on our perceptions and logical summations.

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:40.190
But we are not conscious enough to create
and sustain conclusive overarching answers

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.049
from it all.

00:00:42.049 --> 00:00:47.120
Our most meaningful questions can only be
speculated.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.409
Questions like where we come from.

00:00:50.409 --> 00:00:52.329
Why we are here.

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:54.209
Where we are going.

00:00:54.209 --> 00:00:56.870
And what is the point of it all?

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:03.710
The simple fact is, we currently have no way
of finding answers to these questions.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:08.659
Perhaps these answers do not even exist in
conclusive form.

00:01:08.659 --> 00:01:14.740
Or perhaps humans are not built with the purpose
to ever find them.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:22.229
When reflecting on our inability to conclusively
answer our most basic existential questions

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:29.509
over the last several hundred thousand years
of human existence, it begins to feel hopeless.

00:01:29.509 --> 00:01:36.159
And it is our continuing ignorance of reality
that creates the void that we can never quite

00:01:36.159 --> 00:01:37.159
fill.

00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:48.450
It is why we chase habitual distractions and
temporary pleasures in life.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:52.950
Because what is the point of living without
answers as to why we live at all?

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.610
And furthermore, what is the point of living
without any real prospect for these answers?

00:01:54.610 --> 00:02:02.000
But arguably, not having all of the answers
is the biggest reason to live.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:08.830
As humans, we operate from a system of duality
that cares about logic and understanding as

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:11.819
well as emotion and feeling.

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:18.920
Our purpose and enjoyment of life is not bound
exclusively to a finite endpoint of the pursuit

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:19.920
of knowledge.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:27.930
An endpoint to our questionings and revelations
about reality would be an end to our humanity.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:35.810
It is the perpetual game of cat and mouse
that we play with reality that stimulates

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:39.050
vigor in life.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:42.939
Without it, what would there be to strive
for?

00:02:42.939 --> 00:02:46.500
What would there be to feel emotion over?

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:53.659
The part of human life that is so profoundly
interesting would cease without it.

00:02:53.659 --> 00:02:59.500
We should not live with existential angst
and a constant chip on our shoulder because

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:05.230
we do not and cannot possess definitive answers
to all of our questions.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:10.970
Instead, we should live with the excitement
and wonder that comes from the fact that because

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:18.950
of this, we will always possess the potential
for new discoveries and new worlds of life.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:25.080
We will always be able to create theories
and meaning and experience the awe of their

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.480
realizations.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:33.780
It is deeply human to strive for answers and
to move towards new understandings and explanations.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:42.830
To fantasize about the singularity between
humanity and the reality in which it resides.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:49.329
To visualize an end point of intelligence
and become synchronized with absolute truth.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:54.659
But it is also deeply human to never achieve
this.

00:03:54.659 --> 00:04:00.420
And to believe and depend on this occurring
misses the entire point.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:06.140
The pursuit of understanding and knowledge
can and should exist for itself.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:09.900
This pursuit is what makes us who we are.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:17.631
Excitement, wonder, and humanity itself are
all rooted in the very fact that life, or

00:04:17.631 --> 00:04:21.140
at least our understanding of it, is constantly
in flux.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.231
New possibilities arise with every second
that passes and we must enjoy playing the

00:04:23.231 --> 00:04:26.110
game that this creates, simply for the sake
of playing the game.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:32.690
If we view life in this way, the void we all
have within us will begin to feel a little

00:04:32.690 --> 00:05:02.030
less deep.

